HIKARI STUDIO — QUICK REFERENCE

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
DECISION: Which workflow?
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Almost everything:
  Copy edit, color tweak, spacing, component/responsive adjustment.
  ──→ Use: /quick-site "description of the change"
  (Claude classifies risk, implements, verifies, repairs — one shot.)

Genuinely high-risk or ambiguous scope:
  • Hero image swap  • Header behavior  • Navigation  • Global typography
  • Broad/structural layout change
  ──→ /quick-site will detect this and escalate itself, or start directly:
      scripts/run.sh start "description" (full workflow)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
/quick-site FLOW  (see .claude/skills/quick-site/SKILL.md for full detail)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. You run:  /quick-site "what you want changed"
2. Claude classifies risk, implements the smallest edit, runs:
     scripts/run.sh quick --baseline --risk <level>
     scripts/run.sh quick --verify   --risk <level>
3. Pass → done, concise summary printed.
   Fail → Claude repairs the ONE cause, verifies again (max 3 attempts).
4. Still failing after 3 → escalates to the full workflow below.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
FULL WORKFLOW (high-risk, complex changes)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

scripts/run.sh start "<request>"
# → Claude: write acceptance-criteria.md + expected-files.txt
scripts/run.sh baseline
# → Capture pre-change state
# → Claude: implement the change
scripts/run.sh verify
# → Run all checks, capture after-state
# → Claude: review visual + scope
scripts/run.sh review visual_review pass
scripts/run.sh review acceptance_criteria_pass pass
scripts/run.sh review scope_review pass
# → (repair cycle if needed: fix + run.sh verify again, max 3 times)
scripts/run.sh report
# → Generate final-report.md + final_status

